A class-room teacher is keen to assess the learning of her students on the concept of “relations” taught to them. She writes the following five relations, each defined on the set A = {1, 2, 3} :
R₁ = {(2, 3), (3, 2)}
R₂ = {(1, 2), (1, 3), (3, 2)}
R₃ = {(1, 2), (2, 1), (1, 1)}
R₄ = {(1, 1), (1, 2), (3, 3), (2, 2)}
R₅ = {(1, 1), (1, 2), (3, 3), (2, 2), (2, 1), (2, 3), (3, 2)}

Identify the relation which is reflexive, transitive but not symmetric.

